<Project>
  <!--
    The MSBuild properties the DDDToolkit generators read are declared here. A generator only sees a
    property the project lists as a CompilerVisibleProperty, so the list ships in the package the
    generators ship in: wherever they arrive, this file arrives with them. A new property a generator
    reads goes in this file, not in the package of the integration that happens to use it.

    Packed as build/<package id>.props for a project that references the package itself, and as
    buildTransitive/<package id>.props for one that gets it through another package or project.
    Directory.Build.props imports this same file for the projects in this repository, which reference
    the generators as projects and so never restore the package.

    A property that is declared and not set reaches the generator as an empty value. One that is not
    declared does not reach it at all, which is how the generator tells that this file was not
    imported (DDD00014).

    DDD_Module also declares the project's module, and the generators learn that from the build rather than from
    the property: the package's targets file writes the declaration into the project, where every generator of it
    and of the projects that reference it sees it. DDD_DeclareModule, which a project that sets DDD_Module and is
    meant to be no module sets to false, is read by that step, and the targets file declares it for the generators:
    that it arrives is how they tell the step ran (DDD00064), so it belongs with the step and not here. See
    DDDToolkit.Analyzers.targets.

    The property declared elsewhere is SupabaseMigrationsExport, which switches on a build step:
    DDDToolkit.EntityFramework.Supabase declares it in the targets file that holds the step, with
    IsTestProject and IsTestingPlatformApplication, which keep that step out of test projects, so the step
    and its generator cannot arrive apart, nor decide apart where the step runs. The two marks of a test
    project are declared here as well, for the analyzers of this package; a project that gets both files
    declares them twice, which hands the compiler the same value twice.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Names the generated {Module}EventNames, Add{Module}Converters, Add{Module}IntegrationEvents and
      Add{Module}GraphQlRuntimeBindings, as the module it declares does. [assembly: Module] in the source wins.
    -->
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="DDD_Module" />

    <!--
      Where a diagnostic about the project's module points when no line of its source declares the module: the
      build declared it from DDD_Module, and the file it wrote that into is no one's to edit.
    -->
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="MSBuildProjectFullPath" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Mark a test project: what Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk sets, and what Microsoft.Testing.Platform sets in a test
      application that may lack the first. DDD00061, a handler called directly, is not reported there, where a
      test calls a handler on purpose to test it alone.
    -->
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="IsTestProject" />
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="IsTestingPlatformApplication" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
